    "answer": {
      "short": "Correct answer: C.",
      "worked": "The parabola is concave up, so the coefficient of $x^2$ is positive: A, B or C. The vertex is $(2,-1)$, so check $x=-\\dfrac{b}{2a}$ for each.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{A: }x&=-\\frac{4}{2(1)}=-2\\\\\\text{B: }x&=-\\frac{-8}{2(2)}=2\\\\\\text{C: }x&=-\\frac{-4}{2(1)}=2\\end{align*}$$\nA is eliminated. For B and C, substitute $x=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{B: }y&=2(2)^2-8(2)+3=-5\\\\\\text{C: }y&=2^2-4(2)+3=-1\\end{align*}$$\nOnly C has vertex $(2,-1)$. Correct answer: C.",
